      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit QED turned superconducting circuits into controllable platforms for fundamental light–matter physics and quantum information, with broad influence across the field.",
        "attribution": "Blais and Girvin supplied key theoretical foundations; Schoelkopf led pivotal experimental development. The field was collaborative, so the nominated trio represents central but not necessarily exhaustive credit.",
        "maturity": "The framework and its experimental consequences have been reproduced and extended across many laboratories over decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
