        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The prediction and realization of the quantum spin Hall effect opened topological insulators as a major area of condensed-matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele established the theoretical framework; Molenkamp's experiments demonstrated the effect in a material system.",
        "maturity": "The basic phenomenon is well established, though material disorder and the limits of early realizations remain relevant.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The distinction between the original quantum spin Hall discovery and later topological phases should guide the prize scope."
        ]
      }
    },
